---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { withSiteTitle } from '@utils/seo.js';
---

<Layout
	title={withSiteTitle('Accessibility')}
	description="How No Man's Sky Recipes approaches accessibility: our WCAG 2.2 AA target, known limitations, and how to report a problem."
	slug="accessibility"
	breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Accessibility' }]}
>
	<div class="max-w-3xl pt-4 pb-16 text-ink">
		<Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Accessibility' }]} className="!px-0 mb-4" />
		<h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-bold leading-[1.05] sm:text-5xl">Accessibility</h1>

		<p class="mb-8 max-w-[36rem] text-lg text-dim">
			No Man&apos;s Sky Recipes is a small fan-made site. We want every recipe, item and guide to be usable
			with a keyboard, a screen reader, zoom and other assistive technology.
		</p>

		<div class="max-w-[36rem] space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Our target</h2>
				<p>
					We aim to meet the{' '}
					<a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/" class="link">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a>{' '}
					at level AA. The site is <strong>partially conformant</strong>: most pages meet the target, and the
					known gaps are listed below. We last reviewed the site on 13 October 2026, using automated checks
					(axe-core) and manual keyboard and zoom testing.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">What we do</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-2">
					<li>A &ldquo;Skip to main content&rdquo; link, labelled navigation, and one main heading per page.</li>
					<li>A visible focus outline on every link, button and form field.</li>
					<li>Text contrast of at least 4.5:1, including item names on the game&apos;s colour-coded rarity backgrounds.</li>
					<li>Search, filters and recipe tables announce how many results they found.</li>
					<li>Site search opens as a dialog from the search field in the menu, or with the <kbd>/</kbd> or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> keys. Focus stays inside it until you close it with Escape, then returns to where you were.</li>
					<li>Pages reflow on small screens and at 400% zoom, and animations are reduced when your system asks for less motion.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Known limitations</h2>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-2">
					<li>
						The sortable recipe tables (Refining, Cooking, Crafting and Creature Species) use a third-party
						table library. They work with a keyboard, but screen readers may announce them as a grid with
						extra controls. The card layouts and each item&apos;s own page show the same recipes as plain content.
					</li>
					<li>
						Item colours follow the game&apos;s rarity colours. The colour is never the only way information is
						shown: every item is also named.
					</li>
					<li>
						Wide data tables scroll sideways on small screens instead of reflowing.
					</li>
					<li>
						Advertisements are served by a third party (NitroPay) and are outside our control. If an ad gets in
						your way, please tell us where it appeared.
					</li>
					<li>
						Alliance listings are written by their submitters, so their descriptions and banners may not
						follow these guidelines.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Report a problem</h2>
				<p>
					If something on the site is hard to use, please tell us on the{' '}
					<a href="/feedback/" class="link">feedback page</a>.{' '}
					Include the page address and what you were trying to do, and we&apos;ll try to fix it or get you
					the information another way.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
